#: ../../source/writing-plans_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/writing-plans_SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"Write comprehensive implementation plans assuming the implementer has "
"zero context for the codebase and questionable taste. Document everything"
" they need: which files to touch, complete code, testing commands, docs "
"to check, how to verify. Give them bite-sized tasks. DRY. YAGNI. TDD. "
"Frequent commits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/writing-plans_SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Assume the implementer is a skilled developer but knows almost nothing "
"about the toolset or problem domain. Assume they don't know good test "
"design very well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/writing-plans_SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"**Core principle:** A good plan makes implementation obvious. If someone "
"has to guess, the plan is incomplete."
msgstr ""

